---
description: inference-sandbox project conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

- Stack: Python 3.11, conda env `nvidia`, src layout, pyproject.toml, pytest.
- Hardware target: RTX 5070 Ti / Blackwell sm_120. Verify CUDA, PyTorch, and package versions from the active environment before assuming APIs or wheel support.
- Source code lives under `src/inference_sandbox/`.
- Tests live under `tests/unit/`, `tests/integration/`, and `tests/system/`.
- Keep importable library code separate from CLI scripts and one-off experiments.
- Use `httpx` for HTTP clients; do not introduce `requests`.
- Mark GPU tests with `@pytest.mark.gpu`, Kubernetes tests with `@pytest.mark.k8s`, integration tests with `@pytest.mark.integration`, and slow tests with `@pytest.mark.slow`.
- Never call `.cuda()` directly; use device-agnostic `.to(device)`.
- For timing GPU work, use `torch.cuda.synchronize()` around timed regions.
- Use raw Transformers/PyTorch for correctness baselines, vLLM for OpenAI-compatible serving baselines, and TensorRT-LLM for NVIDIA performance comparisons.
- Cite or verify package versions when proposing API calls. Prefer `python -c`, `pip show <pkg>`, or `python -m pip show <pkg>` before relying on unfamiliar APIs.
- Style: type hints compatible with Python 3.11, Google-style docstrings for public functions, small modules, and ruff-formatted code.